<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00XN">Construction <span data-tag="00XN">3.3.2.5</span> <span class="named">(The $\operatorname{Ex}$ Functor)</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a simplicial set. For every nonnegative integer $n$, we let $\operatorname{Ex}_{n}( X)$ denote the collection of all morphisms of simplicial sets $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Chain}[n] ) \rightarrow X$. By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="00XK" href="/tag/00XK">3.3.2.2</a>, the construction $( [n] \in \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \mapsto (\operatorname{Ex}_{n}(X) \in \operatorname{Set})$ determines a simplicial set which we will denote by $\operatorname{Ex}(X)$. The construction $X \mapsto \operatorname{Ex}(X)$ determines a functor from the category of simplicial sets to itself, which we denote by $\operatorname{Ex}: \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}\rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$. </p>
